# netsurf: polyfill -- on<event> handlers on document and window, document.title, element interfaces keep the element prototype
#
# - React picks its input-event path with ("oninput" in document); false sent
#   every keystroke down an old-IE path that threw "cannot read property 'tag'
#   of null" on each keydown/keyup (claude.ai's email field). Elements had the
#   on<event> properties, document and window did not; the missing ones are
#   now accessors over addEventListener.
# - document.title only returned what script had assigned; it now falls back
#   to the <title> element.
# - The stand-in constructors for element interfaces the bridge lacks
#   (HTMLTitleElement and ~60 more) chained straight to HTMLElement.prototype,
#   skipping the bridge's element class prototype that carries textContent,
#   innerHTML and ~140 more: <title>.textContent was undefined. They now
#   chain through it.
